  "rationale": "Deploy mfa:admin. This blocks both auth_dc and auth_adfs, preventing their footholds and administrator states. Consequently, stolen_dbadmin cannot be obtained, so authentication to the database, fileserver, and backup—and hence every exfiltration technique—is unreachable. With no controls, an attack succeeds via phish_workstation → pivot_internal → auth_appserver → kerberoast_dc → auth_dc → escalate_dc → dump_dbadmin_dc → auth_db → escalate_db → exfiltrate_db. Therefore the minimum is exactly one control."
